      "id": "offgrid-solar",
      "name": "Off-grid cell tower solar & battery",
      "shortName": "Take remote towers off diesel",
      "scope": "Scope 1",
      "ghgCategory": "Stationary Combustion — remote sites",
      "description": "Replacing diesel generators at off-grid rural sites with solar-plus-battery power systems.",
      "owner": {
        "name": "Daniel Osiel",
        "role": "Rural Network Lead",
        "department": "Network"
      },
      "unit": "tCO2e",
      "baseline": 2100,
      "current": 972,
      "target": 900,
      "targetYear": 2027,
      "percentVsTarget": 8.0,
      "status": "stalled",
      "dataStatus": "pending_review",
      "staleDays": 19,
      "lastCheckIn": null,
      "overview": "Forty off-grid sites still run on diesel generators, mostly in the Highlands and mid-Wales network where grid connection isn't viable. The goal is to convert all forty to solar-plus-battery by the end of 2027, cutting roughly 1,200 tCO2e a year and removing ~140,000 litres of diesel resupply trips annually — a real cost story alongside the carbon one.",
      "currentNote": "12 of 40 sites converted so far. The planning consent for REMOTE-1329's battery enclosure was delayed for weeks but cleared on 2026-09-10 — the contractor has mobilised and the two outstanding sites are expected to convert within the week. Diesel volumes haven't moved yet this quarter, which is the flag below.",
